Hi Ista,

Yes, that's it!  I was so caught up in the idea of two steps: 1) create a list of models and 2) apply them for predictions, etc. that I could not get my brain to back up to the single step you show: create the model and use it right away. As Homer would say, "Doh!".

Thanks very much!

Bob

On Tuesday, May 28, 2013 8:01:41 PM UTC-4, izahn wrote:
> Hi Bob,
>
> I hope I'm not missing the point here, but why not keep the original
> data.frame intact throughout the whole process? Doesn't
>
> my_data2 <- ddply(my_data, "group", function(DF) {
>     m <- lm(y ~ x, data=DF)
>     DF$resid <- resid(m)
>     DF$fitted <- predict(m)
>     return(DF)
> })
>
> accomplish your goal?
>
> Best,
> Ista
>
> On Mon, May 27, 2013 at 10:00 AM, Bob <muen...@tennessee.edu> wrote:
