> > use with variables that were not in the original model. I thought this would
> > be simple to do, and it is when the model is not done by group. However
> > adding group changes the order of the cases and I can't figure out how to
> > get them back. An odd thing I learned in the process is that using the
> > "with" function to run a modeling function will cause the case names to be
> > replaced by 1, 2, 3... As you can see below, the "data" argument leaves them
> > intact.
> >
> > The simplified example below demonstrates the problem. I've got to be
> > missing something really simple in this. Any ideas?
> >
> > Thanks,
> > Bob
