> 9   8  8.895382     B  0.09369754  8.801684
> 10 10 10.500953     B -0.44845260 10.949406
>
> The row names appear to get stripped during the data splitting process
> in plyr. However, if you use base R functions, you can get closer to
> what Bob wanted:
>
> regfit <- function(DF)
> {
>     m <- lm(y ~ x, data=DF)
>     DF$resid <- resid(m)
>     DF$fitted <- predict(m)
>     return(DF)
> }
>
> # row names are retained
> my_data3 <- split(my_data, my_data$group)
>
> # group appended ahead of original row names
> do.call(rbind, lapply(my_data3, regfit))
>
>        x         y group       resid    fitted
> A.101  1  3.611557     A  0.26380725  3.347750
> A.103  3  4.349679     A -0.35210563  4.701785
> A.105  5  6.183538     A  0.12771733  6.055821
> A.107  7  7.155509     A -0.25434676  7.409856
> A.109  9  8.978819     A  0.21492781  8.763891
> B.102  2  1.615457     B -0.74306214  2.358519
> B.104  4  5.189158     B  0.68291663  4.506241
> B.106  6  7.068863     B  0.41490057  6.653963
> B.108  8  8.895382     B  0.09369754  8.801684
> B.110 10 10.500953     B -0.44845260 10.949406
>
> At this point, one could use reshape2:colsplit() to extract the
> original row names. OTOH, the equivalent plyr call strips the row
> names again:
>
> > head(ldply(my_data3, regfit))
>    .id  x         y group       resid    fitted
> 1    A  1  3.611557     A  0.26380725  3.347750
> 2    A  3  4.349679     A -0.35210563  4.701785
> 3    A  5  6.183538     A  0.12771733  6.055821
> 4    A  7  7.155509     A -0.25434676  7.409856
> 5    A  9  8.978819     A  0.21492781  8.763891
> 6    B  2  1.615457     B -0.74306214  2.358519
>
> Normally, I prefer plyr's behavior because I've seen some hideous row
> name combinations in split-apply-combine processes using base
> functions, but there are occasions when the row names are meaningful
> (e.g., when the row names are states or countries) and it would be
> useful to have a way in plyr to optionally retain the row names.
> Perhaps Bob can file it as a feature request on plyr's issues page:
> https://github.com/hadley/plyr/issues.
>
> > sessionInfo()
> R version 3.0.1 (2013-05-16)
> Platform: x86_64-w64-mingw32/x64 (64-bit)
>
> locale:
> [1] LC_COLLATE=English_United States.1252
> [2] LC_CTYPE=English_United States.1252
