Hi All,

To follow up on the row.names question, on Github there's much discussion about plyr overwriting row.names, so it's not a bug, it's a feature ;-).  There's a name_rows function to help automate the conversion of row.names to a variable and back, but I don't think it would fix the lm case.names overwrite. However, you'd have to combine that with Ista's approach of merging model results back to the original data to be able to identify outliers, or use R's built in apply functions to get accurate case.names.

Cheers,
Bob

